<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>uav0_track</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version='1.9'>model.sdf</sdf>
  <description>
    Tracker gate variant: airframe + forward RGB camera + forward depth camera +
    ground-truth odometry as a VIO stand-in. No down camera, no lidar, so only
    2 render sensors tick per step (same count as uav0_nav, RTF ~0.999) instead
    of uav0_full's 4, which contend for one render thread and sink RTF below
    0.95 (see uav_sim_gz/README.md Sec 7, plan/P5-perception.md Sec 3b/4).

    The RGB camera stays even though only depth feeds obstacle_extractor_node:
    Gazebo does not bridge a separate camera_info for depth_front, so the
    extractor borrows the RGB one (see uav_perception/README.md,
    obstacle_extractor_node section). Dropping RGB would starve depth of
    intrinsics.
  </description>
</model>
